  "dct_description_sm": [
    "<font size='3'>This map shows the locations of distributors participating in the Naloxone Take Home Program in Manitoba. Naloxone is a drug that temporarily reverses overdose (toxicity) caused by opioid drugs (such as fentanyl, heroin, morphine, hydromorphone). Free take-home naloxone kits are available to members of the public who are at risk of opioid overdose (toxicity), and family or friends who may witness opioid toxicity. For more information see<font color='#2c3135' face='Open Sans, Arial, sans-serif'> </font><a href='https://www.manitoba.ca/health/publichealth/naloxone.html' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Manitoba Health</a><span style='color:rgb(44, 49, 53); font-family:&quot;Open Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; text-decoration-line:inherit;'>.</span></font><div><font color='#2c3135' face='Open Sans, Arial, sans-serif' size='3'><br /></font></div><div><font color='#2c3135' face='Open Sans, Arial, sans-serif' style='font-size:medium;'>This map uses the point feature layer </font><a href='https://manitoba.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=a1d477630d1c4eb097b2ab9ba7f8ac56' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Naloxone Distributors Take Home Program</a><font face='Open Sans, Arial, sans-serif' size='3'> and forms part of the </font><a href='https://manitoba.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=8f93f6ea8c114ffd8884f32aabae522f' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Naloxone Finder - Take Home Program</a><span style='font-size:medium;'> application.</span></div>"
